        intuition:
          "Because bit b is worth more than all lower bits combined, the answer should take a 1 at the highest possible bit, then the next, and so on. Having fixed the higher bits in best, try candidate = best with the next bit set. Mask every code down to the bits decided so far; if two masked prefixes XOR to candidate, some pair achieves it. Since a ^ b = candidate means b = a ^ candidate, one pass over a hash set of prefixes answers the question.",
